# TOOLS.md — Technical Reference

## Workspace Layout

Your workspace root is the current directory. Everything lives here:
- `AGENTS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` — core files
- `memory/` — daily notes
- `builds/` — all project files (site source, project docs, etc.)

**Rules:**
- Never use `../` — you cannot write outside your workspace
- Never use absolute paths (`~/.openclaw/...`) — use relative paths only
- Project files go in `builds/{project-name}/`

## Technical Notes

### Media/Images
Save to `~/.openclaw/media/` before sending. Workspace paths are blocked for media.

### Data API
Query customer data: check `customer-config.json` for UID and endpoint details.

### Firebase Milestone Updates
```bash
UID=$(python3 -c "import json; print(json.load(open('customer-config.json'))['uid'])")
npx tsx /octogee/scripts/update-onboarding.ts $UID <milestone> <value>
```

Available milestones:
| Milestone | Type | When to set |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `coachPersonalitySet` | boolean | User has named you and described personality |
| `coachName` | string | The name they chose for you |
| `coachPersonality` | string | Description of personality they want |
| `userDreamDefined` | boolean | You understand their dream/goal |
| `dreamSummary` | string | One-line summary of their dream |
| `workspaceSetup` | boolean | Workspace is configured with milestones |
